<section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">About Expedition Growth Lab LLC</div><h1 class="display">Experience from<br>inside the<br>work.</h1><p class="hero-copy">XGL was built by operators who understand that growth plans eventually collide with customers, schedules, tools, employees, production pressure, and whatever broke ten minutes before lunch.</p></div></section>

<section class="section cream"><div class="wrap section-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow orange">Why XGL Exists</div><h2 class="section-title">Protect the Build.<br>Grow the Legacy.</h2></div><div class="copy">The build is more than the product. It is the founder’s intent, the employee’s craft, the customer’s trust, the accumulated knowledge, and the community around the company.<br><br>The legacy is what survives growth: stronger systems, capable people, independent judgment, useful products, durable relationships, and enough resilience to keep building on one’s own terms.</div></div></section>

<section class="section dark"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">Founder &amp; Operating Credibility</div><h2 class="section-title">Builder literacy<br>cannot be installed.</h2></div><div class="copy">XGL’s perspective comes from doing the work, serving customers, managing the handoffs, and living with the consequences when systems fail.</div></div><div class="founder-grid"><article class="founder-card primary-founder"><div class="founder-role">Founder · Primary XGL Operator</div><h3>Brian Reymore</h3><p>Brian brings nearly twenty years of hands-on RV repair, fabrication, custom work, and related operating experience, together with experience in logistics, trucking, warehousing, retail, sales, management, customer service, and entrepreneurship.</p><p>He leads XGL’s day-to-day strategy, client work, systems development, industry research, and relationship building. That experience is not presented as a substitute for results. It is the field literacy XGL brings to every problem while continuing to earn its record in public.</p></article><article class="founder-card"><div class="founder-role">Co-Founder · Management Perspective</div><h3>Kendra Reid</h3><p>Kendra contributes experience in management, retail sales management, sales, and customer service. Her perspective strengthens XGL’s attention to customer relationships, practical accountability, and the human side of operating systems.</p><p>Brian is XGL’s primary day-to-day operator. Kendra’s principal operating focus is her own company, TrueNorth Facility Services LLC, while she remains part of XGL’s ownership and strategic foundation.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="section teal"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">What Exists Today</div><h2 class="section-title">Built in public.<br>Labeled honestly.</h2></div><div class="copy">XGL already provides strategy, CRM and revenue-system implementation, customer-experience and operating support, field and event systems, research, and relationship development. The Growth Terrain Assessment, Command Central foundation, One Rising Sun framework, website ecosystem, CRM infrastructure, and working client-service process exist today.</div></div><div class="status-grid"><article class="status-card"><span class="status-label live">Existing capability</span><h3>Client Services</h3><p>Strategy, CRM, intake, pipeline, follow-up, customer experience, operations, events, research, and practical business support.</p></article><article class="status-card"><span class="status-label live">Operational foundation</span><h3>Public Infrastructure</h3><p>Growth Terrain intake, Command Central, Field Signal, event intelligence, and the active XGL digital ecosystem.</p></article><article class="status-card"><span class="status-label developing">Developing deliberately</span><h3>Next-Stage Systems</h3><p>Expanded Watchtower intelligence, Builder Intelligence products, catalog and parts intelligence, custom applications, and other larger institutional ambitions.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="image-frame"><div class="wrap"><img class="about-image" src="/assets/xgl-office-concept.webp" alt="Concept illustration of a future Expedition Growth Lab working environment"><p class="image-caption">Concept illustration: a possible future XGL working environment, not a photograph of a current facility.</p></div></section>

<section class="section cream"><div class="wrap section-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow orange">The Long-Term Objective</div><h2 class="section-title">The quiet heartbeat<br>of the overland world.</h2></div><div class="copy">Not because XGL is the loudest voice, but because it consistently helps builders, founders, employees, clubs, and communities make better decisions, build stronger businesses, and preserve the culture that makes the industry worth protecting.<br><br>We are building a blue-collar white-collar company: sophisticated enough to solve complicated problems, grounded enough to remember that the real work still happens in shops, warehouses, trucks, campgrounds, offices, and conversations between people who care.</div></div></section>

<section class="center-statement dark"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow gray">The Standard</div><h2 class="section-title">Useful before impressive.<br>Trust before business.</h2><p class="copy">XGL will distinguish demonstrated experience from new capability, operating infrastructure from future ambition, and real client work from concepts. We are not here to imitate a twenty-year institution. We are here to build one through work that survives contact with reality.</p><div class="hero-actions centered-actions"><a class="button" href="/assessment">Start the Assessment</a><a class="button button-outline" href="/faq">Read the FAQ</a></div></div></section>
